.SH "TAHWEEL CONVERT"
Convert PDFs and images into TXT, DOCX and JSON with Google Drive OCR.

Inputs can be PDF, JPEG and PNG files, or folders containing them. Every page is recognized, including PDFs that already have a text layer. Pages use grayscale PNG. Image inputs are capped at a 2,339\-pixel long edge without enlargement. Pages over 2,000,000 bytes fall back to JPEG, then shrink to fit.
.PP
\fBUsage:\fR tahweel convert [OPTIONS] <INPUT> ...
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.PP
.TP
\fB\-\-recognizer\fR \fI<BACKEND>\fR
Recognizer to use for the entire run. Required; no automatic switching.
.TP
\fB\-l, \-\-language\fR \fI<LANG>\fR
OCR language code, such as ar or en.
.RS
\fIDefault: \fRar
.RE
.TP
\fB\-r, \-\-recursive\fR
Include files in subdirectories. Directory symlinks are not followed.
.TP
\fB\-q, \-\-quiet\fR
Hide progress bars.
.TP
\fB\-v, \-\-verbose\fR
More logging (\-v debug, \-vv trace). RUST_LOG overrides.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output\-dir\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Directory for outputs; selects tree\-to\-tree mode unless \-\-output\-mode is given.
.TP
\fB\-\-output\-mode\fR \fI<MODE>\fR
Destination layout [default: side\-by\-side without \-o, tree\-to\-tree with \-o].
.TP
\fB\-f, \-\-format\fR \fI<FORMATS>\fR
Output formats, comma\-separated: txt, docx, json or all.
.RS
\fIDefault: \fRall
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-page\-separator\fR \fI<TEXT>\fR
Text between pages in TXT output. Decodes \\n (newline), \\t (tab) and \\\\ (backslash).
.RS
\fIDefault: \fR\\n\\nPAGE_SEPARATOR\\n\\n
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-skip\-existing\fR
Skip documents when every requested output file already exists.
.TP
\fB\-\-dpi\fR \fI<N>\fR
PDF rendering resolution in dots per inch. Must be greater than zero.
.RS
\fIDefault: \fR200
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-pdfium\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
PDFium shared library file. By default, look beside tahweel, then on the system library search path. Needed only for PDF inputs; included in release archives.
.RS
\fIEnvironment: \fR\fBTAHWEEL_PDFIUM\fR
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-service\-account\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
drive\-service\-account: service\-account JSON keys (repeat or comma\-separate). At least one is required.
.RS
\fIEnvironment: \fR\fBTAHWEEL_SERVICE_ACCOUNTS\fR
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-drive\-token\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
drive\-oauth: saved sign\-in file [default: tahweel/google\-token.json in the local data directory, such as ~/.local/share/tahweel/google\-token.json on Linux]. A missing file starts browser sign\-in. Delete this file to sign out.
.TP
\fB\-\-drive\-concurrency\fR \fI<N>\fR
Both Drive recognizers: maximum concurrent pages per account, including cleanup.
.RS
\fIDefault: \fR8
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-drive\-attempts\fR \fI<N>\fR
Both Drive recognizers: attempts per HTTP operation, including the first.
.RS
\fIDefault: \fR5
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-drive\-test\-url\fR \fI<URL>\fR
Test\-only origin for local mock API, upload, token and sign\-in endpoints.
.TP
\fB\-h, \-\-help\fR
Print help
\fBArguments:\fR
.PP
.TP
\fB<INPUT>\fR
PDF, JPEG and PNG files or folders to convert.
\fBExit status:\fR
.PP
.TP
\fB0\fR
Success
.TP
\fB1\fR
Setup, filesystem or other runtime error
.TP
\fB2\fR
Invalid arguments
.TP
\fB3\fR
Finished, but some inputs or documents failed
.TP
\fB130\fR
Interrupted with Ctrl\-C
\fBExamples:\fR
.PP
Mirror a folder of books
.PP
.RS 4
tahweel convert books/ \-\-recognizer drive\-oauth \-r \-o text
.RE
.PP
Convert with a service account
.PP
.RS 4
tahweel convert book.pdf \-\-recognizer drive\-service\-account \-\-service\-account key.json \-f txt,json
.RE
.PP
Skip a book whose outputs already exist
.PP
.RS 4
tahweel convert book.pdf \-\-recognizer drive\-oauth \-\-skip\-existing
.RE
.SH "TAHWEEL COMPLETIONS"
